{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2180-09-12 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2180-09-12 20:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, thanks. I’ve had this bloating and gas for about a week now. I’m belching a lot and passing gas more than usual. It’s uncomfortable, especially after eating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2180-09-12 20:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any nausea or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2180-09-12 20:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just nausea sometimes, no vomiting. I haven’t had fevers, chills, or diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2180-09-12 20:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Given your history with the liver transplant and past abdominal issues, we want to make sure nothing serious is going on. We’ll run some blood tests and get an ultrasound of your liver and blood vessels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2180-09-12 20:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. Is this related to my transplant meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2180-09-12 20:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be. Some immunosuppressants like CellCept can irritate the stomach. We’ll check your tacrolimus levels too—they were a bit high last time, which can cause side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2180-09-12 20:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on the same dose. Should we adjust it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2180-09-12 20:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see what the labs show. For now, we’ll keep your meds as they are until we have more info."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2180-09-13 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood work came back. Your white count is normal, and your liver enzymes are slightly elevated but stable compared to past results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2180-09-13 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that a concern?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2180-09-13 07:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not alarming, but we’ll keep an eye on it. Your CMV viral load was undetectable, which is great—no sign of infection. Blood and urine cultures also came back negative."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2180-09-13 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. What about the ultrasound?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2180-09-13 07:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The Doppler ultrasound showed your liver blood vessels are open and flowing normally. No blockages or clots. Your liver itself looks stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2180-09-13 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not a liver issue?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2180-09-13 07:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Doesn’t look like it. The gas and bloating seem more related to your stomach or intestines. We’re considering an upper endoscopy to check for irritation or inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2180-09-13 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2180-09-13 07:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be sedated, so you won’t feel anything. It’s a quick procedure to look inside your stomach and take small tissue samples if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2180-09-13 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m okay with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2180-09-13 07:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll schedule it for tomorrow morning. In the meantime, we’ll start you on simethicone for the gas symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2180-09-13 07:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What is that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2180-09-13 07:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It helps break up gas bubbles in your stomach and intestines. It’s over-the-counter and very safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2180-09-13 07:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great, I’ll try anything to feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2180-09-14 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Ready for your endoscopy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2180-09-14 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, a little nervous but ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2180-09-14 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be asleep the whole time. We’ll update you when you wake up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2180-09-14 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back in your room. The endoscopy went well. Everything looked normal—no ulcers, no inflammation. We took a few biopsies from your stomach lining just to be thorough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2180-09-14 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2180-09-14 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, very good. No signs of infection like CMV, and no damage from acid or meds. The biopsies will check for subtle changes, but I’m not worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2180-09-14 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Could my celiac disease be acting up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2180-09-14 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your tTG IgA level—it was very low, so no sign of gluten exposure or active celiac disease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2180-09-14 13:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. So what’s causing the gas?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2180-09-14 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We don’t have a clear cause yet. It might be related to your immunosuppressants. We’re going to switch you from Mycophenolate Mofetil to Mycophenolate Sodium—it’s easier on the stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2180-09-14 13:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe after transplant?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2180-09-14 13:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s commonly used. Same active ingredient, just a different formulation. We’ll also lower your tacrolimus dose because your levels were high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2180-09-14 13:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "From 2 mg and 1.5 mg to what?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2180-09-14 13:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll change it to 1.5 mg twice a day. We’ll monitor your levels closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2180-09-14 13:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds manageable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Your labs this morning look stable. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. But what about the gas?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve treated what we can in the hospital. The simethicone should help. Since the endoscopy and labs were normal, we’ll refer you to GI for further outpatient workup—maybe dietary causes or bacterial overgrowth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the biopsies?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Those results will come in a few days. Your primary team will follow up with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. So I stop the old CellCept and start the new one?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Stop Mycophenolate Mofetil, start Mycophenolate Sodium 360 mg twice a day. Keep taking your tacrolimus 1.5 mg twice daily, pantoprazole, lisinopril, and the others as before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And simethicone as needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, up to four times a day for gas. Watch for any new symptoms—fever, severe pain, vomiting—and call your hepatologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll have your discharge papers ready soon. You’re doing well—just keep up with your follow-ups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll see my transplant doctor next week. I’m glad we caught the tacrolimus level."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that was important. High levels can cause side effects, so we’re adjusting it to keep you safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I feel much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. We’ll get you home soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2180-09-15 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call if anything changes."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2180-09-12 20:26:00",
    "admission_end": "2180-09-15 17:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of living donor liver transplant for primary sclerosing cholangitis presented with a week of abdominal discomfort, bloating, nausea, belching, and flatulence. Infectious workup including blood and urine cultures was negative, and CMV viral load was undetectable. Celiac serology showed no evidence of gluten exposure. Doppler ultrasound confirmed patent hepatic vasculature with normal flow. An upper endoscopy revealed normal mucosa with biopsies pending. Her immunosuppressive regimen was adjusted due to high tacrolimus levels and gastrointestinal intolerance: tacrolimus was reduced to 1.5 mg twice daily, and mycophenolate mofetil was switched to mycophenolate sodium. She was started on simethicone for symptom relief. With no acute findings and stable condition, she was discharged home with plans for outpatient follow-up to further evaluate the cause of her persistent abdominal symptoms.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified abdominal pain",
      "Nausea",
      "Eructation",
      "Flatulence",
      "Abdominal distension (gaseous)",
      "Liver transplant status",
      "Primary sclerosing cholangitis",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Long term (current) use of antithrombotics/antiplatelets",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus without complications",
      "Celiac disease",
      "Personal history of nicotine dependence"
    ]
  }
}
